#: ../../desktop/installation.rst:3
msgid "Installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/installation.rst:6
msgid "Download"
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/installation.rst:8
msgid "You can download the latest version of the Nextcloud Desktop Synchronization Client from the `Nextcloud download page`_. Clients are available for Linux, macOS, and Microsoft Windows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/installation.rst:12
msgid "You will also find links to source code archives and older versions on the download page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/installation.rst:16
msgid "Supported server versions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/installation.rst:18
msgid "Each desktop client release supports the latest three stable Nextcloud server major versions at the time of release. See the `Nextcloud Server release schedule`_ for supported major versions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/installation.rst:23
msgid "System Requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/installation.rst:25
msgid "Windows 10+ (64-bits only)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/installation.rst:26
msgid "macOS 12.0+ (64-bits only)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/installation.rst:27
msgid "Linux (Ubuntu 24.04 or openSUSE 15.5 or Alma 8 or ...) (64-bits only)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/installation.rst:29
msgid "For Linux distributions, we support, if technically feasible, the current LTS releases. For BSD, we support them if technically feasible, but we do not test them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/installation.rst:34
msgid "We do not support Citrix."
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/installation.rst:36
msgid "We will do our best to advise Citrix users from the desktop client point of view."
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/installation.rst:37
msgid "We will fix issues that are also reproducible on the standard supported systems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/installation.rst:38
msgid "Everything else is outside of our scope."
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/installation.rst:41
msgid "Install on macOS and Windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/installation.rst:43
msgid "Installation on macOS and Windows is the same as for any other software application: download the program and then double-click it to launch the installation, and then follow the installation wizard. After it is installed and configured the desktop client will automatically keep itself updated; see :doc:`autoupdate` for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/installation.rst:49
msgid "For administrator-focused deployment options such as advanced Windows MSI configuration, non-interactive account provisioning, and command-line wizard preconfiguration, see the Admin Manual chapter on desktop client deployment and setup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/installation.rst:55
msgid "Install on Linux"
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/installation.rst:57
msgid "For Linux, Nextcloud officially provides the desktop client as an AppImage on the `Nextcloud download page`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/installation.rst:60
msgid "Some Linux distributions also provide the Nextcloud desktop client through their package managers. These packages are maintained by the distribution or community, not by Nextcloud. If you prefer a package-managed installation, refer to your distribution's documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/installation.rst:65
msgid "Linux users must also have a password manager enabled, such as GNOME Keyring or KWallet, so that the desktop client can log in automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/installation.rst:69
msgid "Initial setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/installation.rst:71
msgid "After installation, the setup wizard opens. Enter the address you use to access your Nextcloud server in a browser, then click **Log in**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/installation.rst:74
msgid "Server address field and Log in button in the desktop client setup wizard"
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/installation.rst:79
msgid "For the remaining wizard steps, including browser authorization and sync options, see :ref:`desktop-add-account`."
msgstr ""
